  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0:\n- FIXED: the token reaches the HTTP call of every UK v1 and v2 operation, so cancelling stops it\n- FIXED: cancelling a configuration-based call ends Canceled with OperationCanceledException, not Faulted; a timeout stays an Error\n- FIXED: printing ClearbankConfiguration or ClearBankClient (%A, ToString) hides the API token\n- FIXED: a webhook nonce above the Int32 range no longer overflows the response or the EU parse\n- BREAKING: WebHookResponse.Nonce and the EU webhook's Nonce are int64\nv1.1.2:\n- ADDED: Api.getEveryAccountAsync, getEveryTransactionAsync and getEveryAccountTransactionAsync read every page\nv1.1.1:\n- FIXED: the HttpClients made here no longer follow redirects, which sent signatures and payment bodies to the redirect's host; a 3xx answer is an error\nv1.1.0:\n- BREAKING: SwaggerProvider 4.2.1: generated models take and return option for optional strings, Guid for ids, DateTimeOffset for date-times; multi-currency AccountIdentifier kind is an enum\n- CHANGED: FSharp.Core 10.1.401, FSharp.Data 8.2.0, KeyVaultSigning 1.0.13 (async signing-client cache fix)\n- CHANGED: legacy DateTime filters of unspecified kind are sent as UTC\n- FIXED: bundled v1/v2 schemas: response keys with spaces, a non-map examples and query uniqueItems that the OpenAPI reader rejects\n- ADDED: CHAPS v6 customer, institution and return payments (chapsCustomerPaymentAsync, chapsInstitutionPaymentAsync, chapsReturnPaymentAsync, chapsAccount)\n- ADDED: interest-bearing account closure: requestAccountClosureAsync, getAccountClosureAsync\n- ADDED: bundled sterling-v1, cop-outbound-v1, cop-accounts-v1 and chaps-v6 schemas; chaps-v6 amount as double\n- FIXED: payment amounts were formatted with the current culture: under a decimal-comma culture (fi-FI, de-DE) every FPS, SEPA, T2, multi-currency and CHAPS payment failed\n- FIXED: a request that cannot be serialized is an Error, not an exception\n- FIXED: multi-currency payment amounts were float32 (1234567.89 was sent as 1234567.9); PaymentRequestItem amount is now float, sent with two decimals\n- ADDED: RequestSigner: Azure Key Vault, local RSA key, or a SHA-256 digest delegate (AWS KMS) for DigitalSignature\n- ADDED: ClearBankClient over a caller-owned, shared HttpClient; Task-based UK.Api, UK.MultiCurrency.Api and EU.Api with CancellationToken\n- ADDED: UK accounts: get by id, update (status, reason, owner, minimum balance), close\n- ADDED: UK virtual accounts: create, list, list all, get, update, disable\n- ADDED: Bacs Direct Debit mandates: list, cancel, return, collections, unpaid collections; transaction returns; unpaid Direct Debits and unapplied Direct Credits\n- ADDED: per-account and per-virtual-account transactions\n- ADDED: Confirmation of Payee name verification, Secondary Reference Data check, inbound CoP opt-out\n- ADDED: multi-currency payment cancellation\n- ADDED: typed UkWebhook / EuWebhook with webhookTypeUK / webhookTypeEU; createSignedResponseAsync with any signer\n- ADDED: ClearBankResponseException carries the status and body of non-success responses\n- FIXED: multi-currency updateAccount, updateAccountStatus and addCurrency sent Authorization, DigitalSignature and X-Request-Id in the wrong headers\n- FIXED: multi-currency deleteAccount sent no Authorization header\n- CHANGED: the configuration-based functions delegate to the Task API and create their HttpClient when run, not when called",
